==French==

===Etymology===
{{inh+|fr|frm|avec}}, {{m|frm|avecques||with}}, from {{inh|fr|fro|avoc}}, {{m|fro|avoec}}, {{m|fro|avuec||with}}, from an assumed {{inh|fr|VL.|*aboc}}, {{m|la|*abhoc}}, {{m|la|*apud hŏque}},<ref>'''1868''', A. Brachet, ''An etymological dictionary of the French language'', avec.</ref><ref name=a>{{R:fr:TLFi|etym=1}}</ref> from {{der|fr|la|apud||with, near, close to}} + {{m|la|hoc||this}} + {{m|la|-que}}. First used as a replacement for {{cog|la|cum||with}} in {{w|Merovingian}} and {{w|Carolingian}} documents from France. Gradually supplanted Old French {{m|fro|od||with}}, itself from {{m|la|apud}} (''od'' survives however in some dialects in Western France under the form ''d'ot'').<ref name=a/>

Cognate with {{cog|pcd|avuc}}, {{cog|nrf|aveuc}}, {{cog|wa|avou}} and, more distantly, with {{cog|frp|avoi}} (from *''ab hoc'' and not *''abhocque'').

===Pronunciation===
* {{fr-IPA}}
* {{audio|fr|Fr-avec.ogg|audio}}

===Preposition===
{{fr-prep}}

# {{qualifier|accompaniment}} [[with]]
#: {{ux|fr|Je suis revenu '''avec''' lui.|t=I have returned '''with''' him.}}
#: {{ux|fr|Voudriez-vous y aller '''avec''' moi ?|Would you like to come '''with''' me?}}
#: {{ux|fr|Ils m'ont dit qu'ils étaient '''avec''' toi.|They told me that they were '''with''' you.}}
# {{qualifier|manner, instrument}} [[with]]
#: {{ux|fr|Je l'ai fait '''avec''' plaisir.|I did it '''with''' pleasure.}}

===Adverb===
{{fr-adv}}
# {{lb|fr|informal}} [[too]], [[also]]
#: {{ux|fr|Il en est vraiment content. —Bien, moi '''avec'''.|t=He's really happy about it. —Well, me '''too'''.}}

